UPDATE questions SET
  stem = $EXPL$Lawson is a 1/3 partner in Pinnacle Partners and passes away in 2025. At death, Lawson''s partnership interest has an FMV of $500,000 and an outside basis of $200,000. The partnership''s total inside basis is $900,000 (Lawson''s 1/3 share = $300,000). The partnership has a election in effect. Lawson''s heir inherits the interest. What is the heir''s basis adjustment to partnership assets?$EXPL$,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 743(b), death triggers a basis adjustment similar to a sale. The heir receives a stepped-up outside basis to FMV ($500,000) under Section 1014. The 743(b) adjustment equals the new outside basis ($500,000) minus the heir's share of inside basis ($300,000) = $200,000 step-up to partnership assets allocable to the heir. Wrong (B): The adjustment is based on the difference between the new outside basis and the share of inside basis, not the inside basis alone. Wrong (C): Death of a partner is treated as a transfer triggering Section 743(b) when a 754 election is in effect. Wrong (D): The adjustment is positive ($500,000 - $300,000 = $200,000) because FMV exceeds the share of inside basis. (See Section 754.)$EXPL$
WHERE id = 12920;

